-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ג/2 (17.8.2022): העסקת עו"ה, עובדי בעלות, בבתי ספר
-- לחינוך מיוחד מוכרים שאינם רשמיים, בהתאם לרפורמת אופק חדש בשנה"ל תשפ"ג.
-- Ofek Hadash in the recognized-unofficial special-education schools for
-- 2022-23: the owners' and the Ministry's steps, who joins, the work week,
-- part-time and over-full positions, mothers and age hours, principals and
-- deputies, school activities, leaving, promotion, counselors, the grade
-- conversion, the advances until the grade is set, and the attendance clock.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common
IMPORT conventions

-- Time in this file is counted in DAYS from the circular's date, 17 August
-- 2022 (day 0), where a rule has a date.
`17 August 2022` MEANS 0
`30 August 2022` MEANS 13

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ג/2`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, date, reference number, circular number, addressee (owners of recognized-unofficial special-education schools not yet in Ofek Hadash), greeting and subject line; no rule.

§§ `1 מבוא`

-- akn:art_1/p1 Background: in HCJ 148/18 the State undertook to equalize teaching resources in recognized-unofficial special-education schools with the official ones from 2019-20; no rule.
-- akn:art_1/p2 Background: the inter-ministerial team and the Director-General's adoption of its conclusions; no rule.
-- akn:art_1/p3 akn:art_1/p4 akn:art_1/p5 A link to the inter-ministerial team's report; no rule.
-- akn:art_1/p6 Background: Ofek Hadash terms were applied to these schools from 2019-20; no rule.
-- akn:art_1/p8 akn:art_1/p9 The circular's purpose, following circular תש"ף/1 (linked); no rule.

DECLARE `decision` IS ONE OF
    `approving a teaching employee's joining of Ofek Hadash`
    `setting the Ofek Hadash grade and converting the salary`
    `setting the education grade and the teaching seniority`

-- 1 ¶7: the Ministry is the ONLY body that approves joining, sets the
-- grade and converts the salary; it also sets education grade and seniority.
@ref akn:art_1/p7
GIVEN d IS A `decision`
GIVETH A Party
DECIDE `who decides` d IS `the Ministry of Education`

§§ `2 תחומי אחריות ביישום הרפורמה`

-- akn:art_2__para_2-1 The heading "שלב ראשון" and the words "actions by the owner"; the actions are below.

DECLARE `circular 2 action` IS ONE OF
    `submit the owner's undertaking through the portal`
    `check and update the teaching employees' data`
    `direct unregistered employees to open an online file`
    `identify the employees who meet the joining conditions`
    `employ them on Ofek Hadash pay and work week`
    `set the timetable by the Ofek Hadash work week`
    `place all employees in the placement system`
    `transfer the salary interface to the Ministry's contractor`
    `pay by the grade set, deducting the advances` HAS `months paid back to joining` IS A NUMBER
    `reimburse the owner`
    `monitor the undertakings to complete an academic degree`
    `submit a request to the exceptions committee`
    `report working hours by the attendance clock`
    `report working hours manually`
    `pay and deduct by the attendance reports`
    `pay the Ofek Hadash advance` HAS `advance paid` IS A NUMBER
    `check each employee's conditions and decide the joining`
    `set the Ofek Hadash grades`
    `compute the school's Ofek Hadash profile`

-- 2.1(1): until the recognized-institutions regulations (1953) are
-- amended, the owner undertakes to apply Ofek Hadash to its special-
-- education schools, by annex A's form, through the portal, by the
-- deadline. F-2022-23_tashpag_02-a: the deadline is printed as 30.8.2021,
-- a year before the circular; the reading adopted is 30.8.2022.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `circular 2 action`
DECIDE `the owner's undertaking` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `submit the owner's undertaking through the portal`
    WITHIN `30 August 2022`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ג/2 2.1(1): the undertaking to join Ofek Hadash in 2022-23 is due by 30.8"

-- akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p3 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p4 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p5 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p6 Where the undertaking's text is (annex A, linked) and the portal link it is submitted through; the duty is above.

-- 2.1(1) ¶7: the deadline as printed, 30.8.2021.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p7
`the deadline as printed, in days from the circular` MEANS 13 MINUS 365

`the printed deadline year` MEANS 2021

`the undertaking is due before the circular was issued, as printed` MEANS
    `the deadline as printed, in days from the circular` LESS THAN `17 August 2022`
#ASSERT `the undertaking is due before the circular was issued, as printed`


-- 2.1(2): the "teaching staff data" report in the עוש"ר system lists the
-- employees as reported for 2019-20; (א) check they are current and update
-- them through the district; (ב) direct unreported employees, health
-- professions and arts therapists included, to open an online file
-- urgently, as the circular on employment approval requires; then identify
-- those who meet the joining conditions (section 3).
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_a akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p4 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p5
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `circular 2 action`
DECIDE `the owner's data steps` IS
         (PARTY `the employer` MUST `check and update the teaching employees' data`)
    RAND (PARTY `the employer` MUST `direct unregistered employees to open an online file`)
    RAND (PARTY `the employer` MUST `identify the employees who meet the joining conditions`)

-- akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p3 The portal link for opening a file; no rule.

-- 2.1(3): those who meet the conditions are employed on Ofek Hadash pay and
-- work week (section 4). The principal: guide employees through the online
-- file; set their timetable by the Ofek Hadash work week; place ALL
-- employees, in the reform and not, in the placement system (משכית).
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_3 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_3/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_3__cls_1 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_3__cls_2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_3__cls_3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `circular 2 action`
DECIDE `the owner's and the principal's first-stage duties` IS
         (PARTY `the employer` MUST `employ them on Ofek Hadash pay and work week`)
    RAND (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `direct unregistered employees to open an online file`)
    RAND (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `set the timetable by the Ofek Hadash work week`)
    RAND (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `place all employees in the placement system`)

-- akn:art_2__para_2-2 The heading "שלב שני" and the words "the owner will act as follows to set an initial grade"; the actions are below.

-- 2.2(1)-(2): the owner transfers its salary interface to the Ministry's
-- contractor (Unique); once the grade is set, it pays by the grade from the
-- date of joining and deducts the advances (section 15).
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `circular 2 action`
DECIDE `the owner's second-stage duties` IS
         (PARTY `the employer` MUST `transfer the salary interface to the Ministry's contractor`)
    RAND (PARTY `the employer` MUST `pay by the grade set, deducting the advances` `months`)

-- 2.2 ¶2-¶9: the Ministry checks each employee's conditions and decides
-- the joining, sets the grade, computes the school's profile and
-- reimburses the owner — and cannot reimburse without the placement system
-- updated by the Ofek Hadash work week and the salary interface transferred.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p3 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p4 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p5 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p6 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p7 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p8 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p9
GIVEN `placement system updated` IS A BOOLEAN, `salary interface transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `circular 2 action`
DECIDE `the Ministry's actions` `placement system updated` `salary interface transferred` IS
         (PARTY `the Ministry of Education` MUST `check each employee's conditions and decide the joining`)
    RAND (PARTY `the Ministry of Education` MUST `set the Ofek Hadash grades`)
    RAND (PARTY `the Ministry of Education` MUST `compute the school's Ofek Hadash profile`)
    RAND (IF `the Ministry can reimburse the owner` `placement system updated` `salary interface transferred`
          THEN PARTY `the Ministry of Education` MUST `reimburse the owner`
          ELSE FULFILLED)

GIVEN `placement system updated` IS A BOOLEAN, `salary interface transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ministry can reimburse the owner` `placement system updated` `salary interface transferred` IF
    `placement system updated` AND `salary interface transferred`

§§ `3 תנאי ההצטרפות`

-- akn:art_3__para_3-1 The heading "הגדרות".

@desc A teaching employee, as far as sections 3-8 ask.
DECLARE `school employee` HAS
    `recognized teaching seniority`       IS A NUMBER  @desc years of actual teaching recognized for pay seniority (internship, army or national service in teaching not counted)
    `academic`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc an academic degree, or a salary grade equivalent to one approved by the Ministry
    `teaching certificate`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `employee's position fraction`        IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position (1 = 100%)
    `signed the academic-completion undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the exceptions committee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in regular education`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc a teacher in regular (not special) education, for 3.4's bracket
    `health professions or arts therapist` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 3.1.1: new = no recognized years of actual teaching (internship, army or
-- national service in teaching excluded).
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_3-1-1
GIVEN e IS A `school employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a new employee` e IF
    e's `recognized teaching seniority` EQUALS 0

-- 3.1.2: existing = entitled to recognition of years of actual teaching
-- for pay seniority.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_3-1-2
GIVEN e IS A `school employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an existing employee` e IF
    e's `recognized teaching seniority` GREATER THAN 0

-- akn:art_3__para_3-2 The heading of 3.2.

-- 3.2.1: an existing academic joins if certified to teach and at a third
-- of a position or more; one without a certificate may ask the exceptions
-- committee (annex B, through the portal).
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p4 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p5 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p6 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p7
GIVEN e IS A `school employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing academic joins` e IF
        `is an existing employee` e
    AND e's `academic`
    AND (e's `teaching certificate` OR e's `approved by the exceptions committee`)
    AND e's `employee's position fraction` AT LEAST (1 DIVIDED BY 3)

-- akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p8 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p9 The portal link for the exceptions committee's form; no rule.

-- 3.2.1 ¶10-11: without a certificate and with seniority BELOW 25, no
-- promotion until certified; the work and part of the studies are then
-- recognized as 12.2.2 sets out. F-2022-23_tashpag_02-b: 12.2.2 reads
-- "up to 25" and "25 and above".
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p10 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p11
GIVEN e IS A `school employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cannot be promoted until certified under 3.2.1` e IF
    (NOT e's `teaching certificate`) AND e's `recognized teaching seniority` LESS THAN 25

-- akn:art_3__para_3-3 The heading of 3.3.

-- 3.3.1: a non-academic with seniority up to 27 (inclusive) must sign an
-- undertaking to complete an academic degree within four years of signing
-- (annex C) and does not join until he signs. 3.3.2: 28 or more need not
-- sign and is employed on reform terms in any case.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-2
GIVEN e IS A `school employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing non-academic joins` e IF
        `is an existing employee` e
    AND NOT e's `academic`
    AND (e's `recognized teaching seniority` AT LEAST 28 OR e's `signed the academic-completion undertaking`)

-- 3.3.3: the owner monitors compliance with the undertakings.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `circular 2 action`
DECIDE `monitoring the undertakings` IS
    PARTY `the employer` MUST `monitor the undertakings to complete an academic degree`

-- 3.3.4: proof of the degree within four years of JOINING: the salary
-- difference to an academic's, retroactive to joining; later: moved to the
-- academic table without differences. F-2022-23_tashpag_02-c: 3.3.1 counts
-- the four years from SIGNING.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-4 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-4/p2
GIVEN `years from joining to the degree` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `differences retroactive to joining` `years from joining to the degree` IF
    `years from joining to the degree` AT MOST 4

-- Within four years or after them, the teacher moves to the academic
-- teachers' table on completing the degree.
GIVEN `completed the degree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `moves to the academic teachers' table under 3.3.4` `completed the degree` IF
    `completed the degree`

-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-c: the start of the four years and of the
-- differences, by clause. Days are counted from the signing (day 0); by
-- 3.3.1 the teacher does not join before he signs, so joining is on that
-- day or later (annex C asks for its own "date of entry to the reform").
DECLARE `start of the period` IS ONE OF
    `the date of signing the undertaking`
    `the date of joining the reform`

`the four years start, under 3.3.1`       MEANS `the date of signing the undertaking`
`the four years start, under 3.3.4`       MEANS `the date of joining the reform`
`the differences run back to, under 3.3.4` MEANS `the date of joining the reform`
`the differences run back to, under annex C` MEANS `the date of signing the undertaking`

GIVEN `start` IS A `start of the period`, `joined on` IS A NUMBER, `degree on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the degree is in time from` `start` `joined on` `degree on` IF
    CONSIDER `start`
    WHEN `the date of signing the undertaking` THEN `degree on` AT MOST 4 TIMES 365
    WHEN `the date of joining the reform`      THEN `degree on` MINUS `joined on` AT MOST 4 TIMES 365

-- Signed on day 0, joined four months later (day 120, say at the start of
-- the school year), degree on day 1,520: late from the signing, in time
-- from the joining.
`the four-year periods start on different dates` MEANS
        NOT (`the degree is in time from` `the four years start, under 3.3.1` 120 1520
             EQUALS `the degree is in time from` `the four years start, under 3.3.4` 120 1520)
    AND NOT (`the differences run back to, under 3.3.4` EQUALS `the differences run back to, under annex C`)
#ASSERT `the four-year periods start on different dates`

-- 3.4: a new academic in a school that joined joins if certified and at
-- a third of a position or more (half a position in regular education).
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p4 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p5 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p6 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p7
GIVEN e IS A `school employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new academic joins` e IF
        NOT `is an existing employee` e
    AND e's `academic`
    AND e's `teaching certificate`
    AND e's `employee's position fraction` AT LEAST (IF e's `in regular education` THEN 0.5 ELSE 1 DIVIDED BY 3)

§§ `3 Who joins, put together`

GIVEN e IS A `school employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `joins Ofek Hadash` e IF
    `an existing academic joins` e OR `an existing non-academic joins` e OR `a new academic joins` e

-- akn:art_3__para_3-5 The heading of 3.5 (interns).

-- 3.5.1-3.5.3: in a school that joined, interns are employed only on
-- reform terms; the internship year counts only at a third of a position or
-- more; at most two years, in which the degree and the certificate are
-- completed or reform employment ends; it counts for tenure, jubilee grant
-- and recuperation seniority, not for pay seniority or promotion periods.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-1 akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-2
GIVEN `intern's position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `internship years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internship year is recognized` `intern's position fraction` `internship years` IF
    `intern's position fraction` AT LEAST (1 DIVIDED BY 3) AND `internship years` AT MOST 2

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-3
GIVEN p IS A `seniority purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internship counts for` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `pay seniority` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the minimal period for promotion` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `seniority purpose` IS ONE OF
    `pay seniority`
    `the minimal period for promotion`
    `tenure`
    `jubilee grant`
    `recuperation`

-- 3.6: a substitute on weekly hours (not single hours) is employed on the
-- terms of the teacher replaced.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-6 akn:art_3__para_3-6/p2
GIVEN `on weekly hours` IS A BOOLEAN, `replaced teacher in Ofek Hadash` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the substitute is on Ofek Hadash terms` `on weekly hours` `replaced teacher in Ofek Hadash` IF
    `on weekly hours` AND `replaced teacher in Ofek Hadash`

§§ `4 מבנה שבוע העבודה למורים ברפורמה`

-- 4.1: a full-position employee works five days, also in six-day schools.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-1
`working days of a full position` MEANS 5

-- 4.2-4.3: in a special-education primary school (grades 1-6, 1-8 or
-- 1-9), and in grades 1-6 of a multi-stage school, the primary work week —
-- also for an existing teacher whose base was kept at the junior-high 24
-- hours; grades 7-12 of a multi-stage school, the post-primary one.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-2 akn:art_4__para_4-2/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-2/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-3 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p4
GIVEN `in a primary school` IS A BOOLEAN, `grade taught` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on the primary work week` `in a primary school` `grade taught` IF
    `in a primary school` OR `grade taught` AT MOST 6

-- 4.4: primary — 36 hours: 26 frontal, 5 individual (groups of up to 3,
-- content set by the principal), 5 stay hours (work meetings up to 2, and
-- the listed tasks). 4.5: health professions and arts therapists — 3
-- individual, 7 stay, two of which may serve to move between institutions.
-- 4.6: post-primary — 36: 23 frontal, 4 individual, 9 stay (meetings up
-- to 4). 4.7: health professions there — 2 individual, 11 stay.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-2 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-3 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2 akn:art_4__para_4-5 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-6 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-1 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-2 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-3 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_1 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2 akn:art_4__para_4-7 akn:art_4__para_4-7/p2
GIVEN k IS A `work-week kind`
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the work week of` k IS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `special-education primary teacher`                 THEN `work week` 36 26 5 5
    WHEN `special-education primary health professional`     THEN `work week` 36 26 3 7
    WHEN `special-education post-primary teacher`            THEN `work week` 36 23 4 9
    WHEN `special-education post-primary health professional` THEN `work week` 36 23 2 11

DECLARE `work week` HAS
    `week hours`       IS A NUMBER
    `frontal hours`    IS A NUMBER
    `individual hours` IS A NUMBER
    `stay hours`       IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `work-week kind` IS ONE OF
    `special-education primary teacher`
    `special-education primary health professional`
    `special-education post-primary teacher`
    `special-education post-primary health professional`

-- 4.4.4(2), 4.6.4(2): the rest of the stay hours go to the tasks listed;
-- 4.5, 4.7: two of a health professional's stay hours may serve to move
-- between institutions.
@desc The tasks the rest of the stay hours go to.
DECLARE `stay activity` IS ONE OF
    `adapting the curriculum and the environment to the pupil`
    `individual meetings with parents`
    `checking work and tests`
    `preparing for and taking part in committees`
    `planning and guiding the special-education assistants`
    `coordinating with outside bodies for the pupil's inclusion`
    `coordinating for educational continuity`
    `work meetings`

GIVEN a IS A `stay activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a stay hour may be spent on` a IF
    TRUE

`stay hours a health professional may spend moving between institutions` MEANS 2

GIVEN k IS A `work-week kind`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the work-meeting hours at most` k IS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `special-education primary teacher`      THEN 2
    WHEN `special-education post-primary teacher` THEN 4
    OTHERWISE 0

-- Each work week's parts add up to its 36 hours.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN k YIELD (`the work week of` k)'s `frontal hours`
                           PLUS (`the work week of` k)'s `individual hours`
                           PLUS (`the work week of` k)'s `stay hours`
                           EQUALS (`the work week of` k)'s `week hours`)
            (LIST `special-education primary teacher`, `special-education primary health professional`,
                  `special-education post-primary teacher`, `special-education post-primary health professional`)

-- akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p11 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p12 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p13 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p5 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p10 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p11 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p12 akn:art_4/p1 akn:art_4/p2 akn:art_4/p3 Links to the detailed work-week tables; no rule.

§§ `5 העסקה בחלקיות משרה ברפורמה`

-- 5.1-5.2: a teacher at least a third of a position; a health professional may be below.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-1 akn:art_5__para_5-2
GIVEN e IS A `school employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be employed at that fraction in the reform` e IF
    e's `employee's position fraction` AT LEAST (1 DIVIDED BY 3) OR e's `health professions or arts therapist`

-- 5.3: each kind of hours is pro-rated to the fraction; below a third, a
-- health professional (or a teacher of a required subject by special
-- approval) at three frontal hours or fewer teaches frontal hours only, and
-- the fraction is those hours over the base.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-3 akn:art_5__para_5-3/p2 akn:art_5__para_5-3/p3
GIVEN k IS A `work-week kind`, f IS A NUMBER @desc the position fraction
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the part-time work week of` k f IS
    `work week` ((`the work week of` k)'s `week hours` TIMES f)
                ((`the work week of` k)'s `frontal hours` TIMES f)
                ((`the work week of` k)'s `individual hours` TIMES f)
                ((`the work week of` k)'s `stay hours` TIMES f)

GIVEN `single frontal hours` IS A NUMBER, `position base` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the fraction of single frontal hours` `single frontal hours` `position base` IS
    `single frontal hours` DIVIDED BY `position base`

-- 5.4: no more than two schools, and no more than 100% in all employments
-- (one school or two) — not for health professionals or a subject the
-- Ministry allows in more schools. F-2022-23_tashpag_02-d: section 6
-- allows more than 100% by exception.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-4
GIVEN `schools` IS A NUMBER, `total fraction` IS A NUMBER, `exempt from 5.4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within 5.4` `schools` `total fraction` `exempt from 5.4` IF
    `exempt from 5.4` OR (`schools` AT MOST 2 AND `total fraction` AT MOST 1)

-- 5.5: work below a third of a position in the reform does not count for
-- the required period for promotion.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-5
GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the period counts for promotion` f IF
    f AT LEAST (1 DIVIDED BY 3)

§§ `6 העסקה מעל 100% משרה ברפורמה`

-- 6.1-6.4: as a rule up to 100%. By exception (not principals or first
-- deputies), for system needs: required subjects (sciences, English,
-- maths, PE), a shortage in the area, a remote locality; the extra hours
-- frontal only; at most 8.5 hours a day and 42 a week. The placement
-- system allows up to 117%; beyond that, headquarters approval.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-1 akn:art_6__para_6-2 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p2 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p3 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p4 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p5 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p6 akn:art_6__para_6-3 akn:art_6__para_6-4
GIVEN `total fraction` IS A NUMBER
      `principal or first deputy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a criterion of 6.2 is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a required subject, a shortage in the area or a remote locality
      `extra hours all frontal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `most hours in a day` IS A NUMBER
      `hours in the week` IS A NUMBER
      `headquarters approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the position may be approved` `total fraction` `principal or first deputy` `a criterion of 6.2 is met` `extra hours all frontal` `most hours in a day` `hours in the week` `headquarters approved` IF
    IF `total fraction` AT MOST 1
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE     NOT `principal or first deputy`
         AND `a criterion of 6.2 is met`
         AND `extra hours all frontal`
         AND `most hours in a day` AT MOST 8.5
         AND `hours in the week` AT MOST 42
         AND (`total fraction` AT MOST 1.17 OR `headquarters approved`)

-- akn:art_6__para_6-4/p2 A link to the guidance on exceptional employment; no rule.

-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-d: one teacher, one school, 110% approved under
-- section 6: 5.4 says no, 6 says yes.
`5.4 and section 6 disagree on an approved 110% in one school` MEANS
    NOT (`within 5.4` 1 1.1 FALSE
         EQUALS `the position may be approved` 1.1 FALSE TRUE TRUE 8 40 FALSE)
#ASSERT `5.4 and section 6 disagree on an approved 110% in one school`

§§ `7 עו"ה אם`

-- 7.1: a mother's position per the takanon: a teaching employee employed
-- at 79% or more in all her employment.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-1 akn:art_7__para_7-1/p2
GIVEN `a mother` IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to a mother's position` `a mother` f IF
    `a mother` AND f AT LEAST 0.79

-- 7.2: a mother reduces one frontal hour and one stay hour. 7.3: after
-- maternity leave, at 90% or more, for four months: one nursing hour a day
-- from the stay hours (five a week), and NOT 7.2 meanwhile. 7.4: at 79% to
-- 90%, 7.2's reduction. 7.5: never both at once. F-2022-23_tashpag_02-e:
-- 90% is in both 7.3 and 7.4; read as 7.3's ("90% ומעלה").
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-2 akn:art_7__para_7-2/p2 akn:art_7__para_7-3 akn:art_7__para_7-4 akn:art_7__para_7-5
GIVEN `a mother` IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A NUMBER, `within four months of maternity leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `hours reduction`
DECIDE `the weekly reduction` `a mother` f `within four months of maternity leave` IS
    IF `within four months of maternity leave` AND f AT LEAST 0.9
    THEN `hours reduction` 0 5
    ELSE IF `entitled to a mother's position` `a mother` f
         THEN `hours reduction` 1 1
         ELSE `hours reduction` 0 0

DECLARE `hours reduction` HAS
    `frontal reduced`  IS A NUMBER
    `stay reduced`     IS A NUMBER

-- The two clauses' own ranges, as printed.
GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in 7.3's range` f IF f AT LEAST 0.9
GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in 7.4's range` f IF f AT LEAST 0.79 AND f AT MOST 0.9

`90% is in both 7.3 and 7.4` MEANS `in 7.3's range` 0.9 AND `in 7.4's range` 0.9
#ASSERT `90% is in both 7.3 and 7.4`

§§ `8 מורים הזכאים לשעות גיל`

-- 8.1: the age of entitlement is unchanged from pre-reform. 8.2: existing
-- and new teachers aged 50-55: 2 frontal hours less, base 34. 8.3: existing
-- teachers 55 and over: 3 frontal and 1 individual less, base 32. 8.4: new
-- teachers 55 and over: 2 frontal only, base 34. Pro-rated for part time.
-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-f: 8.2 and 8.3 both take an existing teacher of 55;
-- read as 8.3's.
@ref akn:art_8__para_8-1 akn:art_8__para_8-2 akn:art_8__para_8-3 akn:art_8__para_8-4 akn:art_8__para_8-4/p2
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, existing IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position base for age` age existing IS
    IF age AT LEAST 55 AND existing THEN 32
    ELSE IF age AT LEAST 50 THEN 34
         ELSE 36

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, existing IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the bases the clauses give` age existing IS
    concat (LIST (IF age AT LEAST 50 AND age AT MOST 55 THEN LIST 34 ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF age AT LEAST 55 AND existing THEN LIST 32 ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF age AT LEAST 55 AND NOT existing THEN LIST 34 ELSE EMPTY))

`an existing teacher of 55 has two bases` MEANS
    `the bases the clauses give` 55 TRUE EQUALS LIST 34, 32
#ASSERT `an existing teacher of 55 has two bases`

§§ `9 מבנה שבוע העבודה למנהלים וסגנים ראשונים`

-- 9.1-9.2: principal and first deputy at exactly 100%, five days; the
-- principal's week 40 hours, 6-9 frontal by complexity.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-1 akn:art_9__para_9-2
`a principal's or first deputy's position fraction` MEANS 1
`a principal's week hours` MEANS 40

-- 9.3-9.4: the school's complexity level (8 levels, by the school
-- management index; at least 3 in special education) sets the principal's
-- and first deputy's teaching hours and pay.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-3 akn:art_9__para_9-4
GIVEN `computed level` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the complexity level of a special-education school` `computed level` IS
    max 3 (min 8 `computed level`)

-- 9.5-9.6: computed early in May of the year before; a new institution,
-- in December of its year, at the minimum until then and retroactively after.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-5 akn:art_9__para_9-6
GIVEN `existed in May of the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN, `level computed in May` IS A NUMBER, `level computed in December` IS A NUMBER, `computed in December yet` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the complexity level for the year` `existed in May of the previous year` `level computed in May` `level computed in December` `computed in December yet` IS
    IF `existed in May of the previous year`
    THEN `level computed in May`
    ELSE IF `computed in December yet` THEN `level computed in December` ELSE 3

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-6/p2 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p3 akn:art_9__para_9-6/t1
`the principal's frontal hours by level` MEANS
    LIST `level row` 3 9, `level row` 4 8, `level row` 5 8, `level row` 6 7, `level row` 7 7, `level row` 8 6

DECLARE `level row` HAS
    `level`        IS A NUMBER
    `level hours`  IS A NUMBER

-- akn:art_9__para_9-6/p4 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p5 A link on computing complexity; no rule.

-- 9.7: the first deputy's week is 40 hours.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7
`a first deputy's week hours` MEANS 40

-- 9.7.1-9.7.3: frontal hours by level in a primary (18-21), post-primary
-- (9-11) and multi-stage (13-15) school.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-1 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-1/t1
`the primary first deputy's frontal hours by level` MEANS
    LIST `level row` 3 21, `level row` 4 21, `level row` 5 20, `level row` 6 20, `level row` 7 19, `level row` 8 18

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-2 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-2/t1
`the post-primary first deputy's frontal hours by level` MEANS
    LIST `level row` 3 11, `level row` 4 11, `level row` 5 11, `level row` 6 11, `level row` 7 9, `level row` 8 9

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-3 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-3/t1
`the multi-stage first deputy's frontal hours by level` MEANS
    LIST `level row` 3 15, `level row` 4 15, `level row` 5 14, `level row` 6 14, `level row` 7 13, `level row` 8 13

-- 9.8: a second deputy works a teacher's week, the individual hours on
-- the deputy's work.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-8
GIVEN k IS A `work-week kind` @desc the teacher's week of the school (primary or post-primary)
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `a second deputy's work week` k IS
    `the work week of` k

-- 9.9-9.10: a principal or first deputy entitled to a mother's position,
-- or aged 50 or more, has two weekly non-frontal hours less, position and
-- pay unchanged.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-9 akn:art_9__para_9-10
GIVEN `a mother's position` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a principal's non-frontal hours reduced` `a mother's position` age IS
    (IF `a mother's position` THEN 2 ELSE 0) PLUS (IF age AT LEAST 50 THEN 2 ELSE 0)

§§ `10 שעות פעילות בית ספרית`

-- 10.1: an employee on reform terms, at any position, is paid for school
-- activities on top of the position and the fixed salary.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-1
GIVEN `employed on reform terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid for school-activity hours on top of the position` `employed on reform terms` IF
    `employed on reform terms`

-- 10.2-10.3: allocated by the school's needs, at most 18 a half-year; for
-- a general school meeting (up to 4), individual parent-and-child meetings
-- (up to 8) and after-hours activity (up to 6).
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-2 akn:art_10__para_10-3 akn:art_10__para_10-3/p2 akn:art_10__para_10-3/p3 akn:art_10__para_10-3/p4
GIVEN `meeting hours` IS A NUMBER, `parent hours` IS A NUMBER, `after-hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a half-year's activity hours are within the caps` `meeting hours` `parent hours` `after-hours` IF
        `meeting hours` AT MOST 4
    AND `parent hours` AT MOST 8
    AND `after-hours` AT MOST 6
    AND `meeting hours` PLUS `parent hours` PLUS `after-hours` AT MOST 18

-- The three caps add up to 10.2's 18.
#ASSERT 4 PLUS 8 PLUS 6 EQUALS 18

§§ `11 יציאה מאופק חדש`

-- 11.1-11.4: all who meet the conditions must join; by exception, for
-- health (own or first-degree family, with current certificates) or
-- humanitarian reasons, a request to leave on annex D's form, through the portal.
@ref akn:art_11__para_11-1 akn:art_11__para_11-2 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p2 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p3 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p4 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p5 akn:art_11__para_11-3 akn:art_11__para_11-4
GIVEN `meets the conditions` IS A BOOLEAN, `health reason` IS A BOOLEAN, `humanitarian reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may ask to leave Ofek Hadash` `meets the conditions` `health reason` `humanitarian reason` IF
    `meets the conditions` AND (`health reason` OR `humanitarian reason`)

-- akn:art_11__para_11-4/p2 The portal link; no rule.

§§ `12 קידום בדרגות`

-- 12.1: promotion needs the required period (פז"נ), professional-
-- development hours (שפ"מ) and an evaluation per the Ministry.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-1 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p4
GIVEN s IS A `promotion step`, months IS A NUMBER, hours IS A NUMBER, `evaluated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be promoted` s months hours `evaluated` IF
    months AT LEAST s's `months required` AND hours AT LEAST s's `development hours` AND `evaluated`

DECLARE `promotion step` HAS
    `step`             IS A STRING
    `months required`  IS A NUMBER
    `development hours` IS A NUMBER
    `raise`            IS A NUMBER

-- akn:art_12__para_12-1/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p6 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p7 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p8 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p9 Links on evaluation and the index map; no rule.
-- akn:art_12__para_12-2 The heading of 12.2.

-- 12.2.1: academics certified to teach.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/t1
`the steps for certified academic teachers` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` "1-2" 30 120 0.075, `promotion step` "2-3" 30 120 0.075,
         `promotion step` "3-4" 36 180 0.075, `promotion step` "4-5" 36 180 0.075,
         `promotion step` "5-6" 36 180 0.075, `promotion step` "6-7" 48 210 0.075,
         `promotion step` "7-8" 48 210 0.075, `promotion step` "8-9" 48 210 0.075

-- 12.2.2: academics not certified. Existing ones "up to 25" years who
-- joined by exception are not promoted until certified, then the period
-- counts from joining for one promotion and up to 60 study hours count as
-- development hours; "25 and above" need not certify. New ones by exception
-- start accruing at certification. F-2022-23_tashpag_02-b: year 25 is in
-- both groups; the reading adopted is 3.2.1's "below 25".
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p6 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p7
GIVEN e IS A `school employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an uncertified academic may be promoted` e IF
    e's `teaching certificate` OR (`is an existing employee` e AND e's `recognized teaching seniority` AT LEAST 25)

`study hours that count as development hours, at most` MEANS 60

-- ¶3-4: for an existing one, the period counted from joining earns one
-- promotion only. ¶7: a new one gets neither benefit and accrues from
-- certification.
`promotions the period from joining may earn` MEANS 1

GIVEN e IS A `school employee`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `an uncertified academic's period for promotion counts from` e IS
    IF `is an existing employee` e
    THEN "employment under the reform"
    ELSE "certification"

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
DECIDE `what 12.2.2's two groups say of seniority` n IS
    append (IF n AT MOST 25 THEN LIST FALSE ELSE EMPTY) (IF n AT LEAST 25 THEN LIST TRUE ELSE EMPTY)

`12.2.2 gives 25 years both answers` MEANS
    `what 12.2.2's two groups say of seniority` 25 EQUALS LIST FALSE, TRUE
#ASSERT `12.2.2 gives 25 years both answers`

-- 12.2.3: certified non-academics: up to 27 years (inclusive) sign the
-- undertaking (3.3) and are not promoted until the degree; 28 and above
-- need not, and are promoted by the table.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/t1 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/t1
`the steps for certified non-academic teachers of 28 years` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` "1-2" 48 480 0.075, `promotion step` "2-3" 48 480 0.075,
         `promotion step` "3-4" 48 480 0.075, `promotion step` "4-5" 48 480 0.075,
         `promotion step` "5-6" 48 480 0.075, `promotion step` "6-7" 48 480 0.075,
         `promotion step` "7-8" 48 480 0.075, `promotion step` "8-9" 48 480 0.075

GIVEN e IS A `school employee`, `degree proven` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a non-academic may be promoted` e `degree proven` IF
    e's `recognized teaching seniority` AT LEAST 28 OR `degree proven`

-- akn:art_12__para_12-3 The heading of 12.3.

-- 12.3.1-12.3.2: principals and deputies — certified academics; certified
-- non-academics of 28 years or more.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/t1 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1/t1
`the steps for certified academic principals and deputies` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` "א-ב" 36 210 0.0875, `promotion step` "ב-ג" 36 210 0.0875, `promotion step` "ג-ד" 36 210 0.0875

@ref akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/t1 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2/t1
`the steps for certified non-academic principals and deputies of 28 years` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` "א-ב" 48 480 0.0875, `promotion step` "ב-ג" 48 480 0.0875, `promotion step` "ג-ד" 48 480 0.0875

§§ `13 יועצים חינוכיים`

-- 13.1: a counselor's week is an academic teacher's, with the frontal
-- hours split between teaching and counseling by the principal, individual
-- hours as counseling, stay hours also for counseling; in primary and junior
-- high at least a sixth of the position in frontal teaching (6 of 36),
-- and not less than 4 frontal hours whatever the position.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-1 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p3 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p4 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p5 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p6 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p7 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p8 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p9
-- The sixth is stated for primary schools and junior highs. Whether that
-- place governs the 4-hour floor too the sentence does not settle
-- (F-2022-23_tashpag_02-i); the floor, "for any position fraction", is read
-- as general, so a counselor elsewhere (a post-primary school, §4.6) needs
-- the 4 hours and not the sixth.
GIVEN `teaching hours` IS A NUMBER, `position hours` IS A NUMBER, `in a primary school or junior high` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a counselor teaches enough` `teaching hours` `position hours` `in a primary school or junior high` IF
    IF `in a primary school or junior high`
    THEN `teaching hours` AT LEAST `position hours` DIVIDED BY 6 AND `teaching hours` AT LEAST 4
    ELSE `teaching hours` AT LEAST 4

-- 13.2: new counselors are on the new combined-salary tables of academic
-- teachers.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-2
GIVEN `a new counselor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on the new academic teachers' combined-salary tables` `a new counselor` IF
    `a new counselor`

-- 13.3: at least seven counseling hours: 8% (temporary licence), 12%
-- (permanent).
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-3 akn:art_13__para_13-3/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-3/p3
GIVEN `counseling hours` IS A NUMBER, `permanent licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the counseling allowance rate` `counseling hours` `permanent licence` IS
    IF `counseling hours` AT LEAST 7
    THEN (IF `permanent licence` THEN 0.12 ELSE 0.08)
    ELSE 0

§§ `14 קביעת הדרגה באופק חדש`

-- 14.1: the Ministry alone sets the grade.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-1
`who sets the Ofek Hadash grade` MEANS `the Ministry of Education`

-- 14.2-14.4: from employment, education and salary data of March of the
-- year before joining, the salary being what is due at 100% for the roles
-- held.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-2 akn:art_14__para_14-3 akn:art_14__para_14-4
`the month whose salary the conversion uses` MEANS "March of the year before joining"

-- 14.5: the grade may be a half grade.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-5
GIVEN `grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a grade the conversion may give` `grade` IF
    `grade` TIMES 2 EQUALS FLOOR (`grade` TIMES 2)

-- akn:art_14__para_14-6 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p3 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p4 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p5 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p6 Further information to follow, a pointer to annex E and links to the tables and the 2016 shekel-supplement circular; no rule.

-- 14.7: the role allowances in Ofek Hadash, at most two per employee.
-- The special-education allowance is "as customary today", which the
-- circular does not state, and "רכז שכבה* 6% / 7%" gives two rates under
-- an asterisk whose note the circular does not carry, and no rule to choose
-- (F-2022-23_tashpag_02-h): both are inputs.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-7 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p3 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p4 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p5 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p6 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p7 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p8 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p9 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p10 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p11 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p12 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p13 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p14 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p15
GIVEN r IS A `role`
      `grade coordinator's rate` IS A NUMBER @desc the grade coordinator's rate: the circular prints "6% / 7%" with an asterisk whose note it does not carry, and no rule for choosing
      `special-education rate customary today` IS A NUMBER @desc the special-education rate as paid today, which the circular does not state
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the role allowance rate` r `grade coordinator's rate` `special-education rate customary today` IS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `second deputy principal` THEN 0.13
    WHEN `class educator` THEN 0.10
    WHEN `first-grade class educator` THEN 0.115
    WHEN `special-education teacher` THEN `special-education rate customary today`
    WHEN `subject coordinator, primary` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `subject coordinator, junior high` THEN 0.08
    WHEN `road-safety coordinator` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `security coordinator` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `social education, primary` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `social education, junior high` THEN 0.10
    WHEN `grade coordinator` THEN `grade coordinator's rate`
    WHEN `laboratory coordinator` THEN 0.03
    WHEN `measurement and evaluation coordinator` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `trips coordinator` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `inclusion coordinator` THEN 0.06
    WHEN `pedagogical coordinator` THEN 0.06

@desc The roles section 14.7 lists.
DECLARE `role` IS ONE OF
    `second deputy principal`
    `class educator`
    `first-grade class educator`
    `special-education teacher`
    `subject coordinator, primary`
    `subject coordinator, junior high`
    `road-safety coordinator`
    `security coordinator`
    `social education, primary`
    `social education, junior high`
    `grade coordinator`
    `laboratory coordinator`
    `measurement and evaluation coordinator`
    `trips coordinator`
    `inclusion coordinator`
    `pedagogical coordinator`

-- A mentor: 2.4% per intern, up to three.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-7/p16
GIVEN `interns mentored` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the mentor's allowance rate` `interns mentored` IS
    0.024 TIMES min `interns mentored` 3

-- At most two role allowances to an employee.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-7/p17
`role allowances an employee may receive, at most` MEANS 2

§§ `15 מקדמות שכר באופק חדש עד לקביעת הדרגה`

-- 15.1: until the grade is set, an advance on top of the current salary,
-- computed on its components (combined salary, the '87 and '94
-- supplements, supplements 2001, 2008 and 2011, the split, development and
-- double-degree allowances), only for the fraction in the joined school and
-- from the joining date; called "מקדמת אופק חדש". Once the grade is set,
-- pay is recomputed back to joining and what was paid, advance included, is offset.
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-1 akn:art_15__para_15-1/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-1/p3
GIVEN `rate` IS A NUMBER, `current components` IS A NUMBER @desc the month's current salary in the listed components, for the fraction in the joined school
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Ofek Hadash advance` `rate` `current components` IS
    `rate` TIMES `current components`

-- ¶3: once the grade is set, Ofek pay back to joining, less the pay and
-- the advances paid since then.
GIVEN `Ofek salary from joining` IS A NUMBER, `salary paid from joining` IS A NUMBER, `advances paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the arrears once the grade is set` `Ofek salary from joining` `salary paid from joining` `advances paid` IS
    `Ofek salary from joining` MINUS (`salary paid from joining` PLUS `advances paid`)

-- 15.2: the rates — primary (and grades 1-6 of a multi-stage school):
-- 17%, interns 14%; post-primary (and grades 7+): 27%, interns 22%;
-- first deputies 20%, principals 15%.
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-2 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p3 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p4 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p5 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p6 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p7 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p8 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p9 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p10
GIVEN g IS AN `advance group`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the advance rate of` g IS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `primary teacher`      THEN 0.17
    WHEN `primary intern`       THEN 0.14
    WHEN `post-primary teacher` THEN 0.27
    WHEN `post-primary intern`  THEN 0.22
    WHEN `first deputy`         THEN 0.20
    WHEN `principal`            THEN 0.15

DECLARE `advance group` IS ONE OF
    `primary teacher`
    `primary intern`
    `post-primary teacher`
    `post-primary intern`
    `first deputy`
    `principal`

-- akn:art_15/p1 Guidance on reimbursing the advance is to come in a separate circular; no rule.

§§ `16 שעון הנוכחות בביה"ס`

-- 16.1-16.4: an attendance clock "is installed" (no one is named:
-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-l) and employees report by it;
-- hours count from clocking in, not before 7:45; manual reports until it is
-- installed; the owner pays and deducts by the reports, after checking
-- justified absences.
@ref akn:art_16__para_16-1 akn:art_16__para_16-3 akn:art_16__para_16-4
GIVEN `the clock is installed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `circular 2 action`
DECIDE `the attendance clock` `the clock is installed` IS
         (IF `the clock is installed`
          THEN PARTY `the teaching employee` MUST `report working hours by the attendance clock`
          ELSE PARTY `the teaching employee` MUST `report working hours manually`)
    RAND (PARTY `the employer` MUST `pay and deduct by the attendance reports`)

@ref akn:art_16__para_16-2
GIVEN `clock-in, in minutes after midnight` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `work counts from` `clock-in, in minutes after midnight` IS
    max `clock-in, in minutes after midnight` (7 TIMES 60 PLUS 45)

-- §17: the circular collects the
-- agreements' rules; where they conflict, the agreements govern, for or
-- against the employee.
@ref akn:art_17
GIVEN `the circular and an agreement conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `which governs` `the circular and an agreement conflict` IS
    IF `the circular and an agreement conflict` THEN "the collective agreements" ELSE "this circular"

-- akn:art_17/p2 akn:art_17/p3 akn:art_17/p4 akn:art_17/p5 akn:art_17/p6 akn:art_17/p7 akn:art_17/p8 akn:art_17/p9 akn:art_17/p10 akn:art_17/p11 akn:art_17/p12 akn:art_17/p13 akn:art_17/p14 akn:art_17/p15 akn:art_17/p16 akn:art_17/p17 akn:art_17/p18 akn:art_17/p19 akn:art_17/p20 akn:art_17/p21 akn:art_17/p22 akn:art_17/p23 akn:art_17/p24 akn:art_17/p25 akn:art_17/p26 akn:art_17/p27 akn:art_17/p28 akn:art_17/p29 akn:art_17/p30 akn:art_17/p31 akn:art_17/p32 The sign-off, signatories and list of copies, which close §17; no rule.

§§ `Annexes`

-- akn:att_1__hc_1 Annex A, the owner's undertaking to apply Ofek Hadash from 2022-23 (its terms and the sanctions up to the licence), and its signature lines; the duty to submit it is 2.1(1).
-- akn:att_2__hc_1 Annex B, the request form for exceptional joining of an academic without a teaching certificate; the rule is 3.2.1.
-- akn:att_3__hc_1 Annex C, the non-academic's declaration and undertaking to complete a degree; the rule is 3.3. (Its ¶9-¶10 date the four years and the differences from signing; F-2022-23_tashpag_02-c.)
-- akn:att_4__hc_1 Annex D, the request form to the exceptions committee to leave Ofek Hadash; the rule is 11.

-- Annex E ¶1-¶5: an existing teacher's grade is set by converting the
-- salary (by personal data, roles and stage before joining); a new one is
-- placed directly at grade 1 by education and role, with no conversion;
-- the Ministry alone sets grades. 1(ד), note 1: a new academic (after the
-- internship) is placed at grade 1 and seniority 1, without conversion.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1 akn:att_5__hc_1/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1/p5 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_1
GIVEN existing IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the salary is converted` existing IF existing

-- 1(א): for an existing teacher, A = X × (100 + Y)%.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a
GIVEN X IS A NUMBER @desc the salary for conversion, at a full position
      Y IS A NUMBER @desc the conversion coefficient, in percent (e.g. 34)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the converted salary` X Y IS
    X TIMES (100 PLUS Y) DIVIDED BY 100

-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p5 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p6 The formula's symbols, encoded above.

-- 1(ב): X is the salary the teacher was entitled to at 100% by the roles
-- held, in March of the school year before the move, in the components
-- listed and the role allowances that do not go on; the joining month if
-- there was no March employment.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b
GIVEN `components at the position held` IS A NUMBER, `position factor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary to convert` `components at the position held` `position factor` IS
    `components at the position held` DIVIDED BY `position factor`

GIVEN `employed in the March before joining` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the month X is taken from` `employed in the March before joining` IS
    IF `employed in the March before joining`
    THEN "March of the school year before joining"
    ELSE "the month of joining"

-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p7 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p8 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p9 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p10 A page letterhead inside the annex; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p11 The heading of the academic conversion coefficients, whose table the corpus does not carry (see below).

-- Y: a non-academic's is the academic's times 0.8; a teacher in grades
-- 7-9 of a primary school on a 24-hour base, plus 12.5% (and works the
-- primary week). The academic coefficients table (page 30) is an image the
-- corpus does not carry (a corpus defect), so the academic Y is an input.
-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-k: "מקדם ההמרה יגדל ב-12.5%" is 12.5% of itself or
-- 12.5 points. The reading adopted, as in every circular that prints this
-- sentence: 12.5% of the coefficient, Y × 1.125.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p12 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p13 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p14
GIVEN `academic coefficient` IS A NUMBER, academic IS A BOOLEAN, `grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the conversion coefficient` `academic coefficient` academic `grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` IS
    `academic coefficient`
    TIMES (IF academic THEN 1 ELSE 0.8)
    TIMES (IF `grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` THEN 1 `increased by` 12.5% ELSE 1)

GIVEN `academic coefficient` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the coefficient grown by 12.5 points` `academic coefficient` IS
    `academic coefficient` PLUS 12.5

`the two readings of 12.5% differ` MEANS
    NOT (`the conversion coefficient` 24 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the coefficient grown by 12.5 points` 24)
#ASSERT `the two readings of 12.5% differ`

-- 1(ב) ¶15-¶31, 1(ג): the teacher's example (a mother teaching in junior
-- high, position factor 0.9, Y = 34): the components and the steps.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p15 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p16 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p17 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p18 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/t1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p19 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p20 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p21 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_c akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_c/p2
`the teacher's components` MEANS
    LIST 3779.38, 141.21, 113.38, 187.25, 259.08, 157.03, 268.82, 900.54, 298.69
`the teacher's stated total`          MEANS 6105.38
`the teacher's position factor`       MEANS 0.9
`the teacher's stated full-position X` MEANS 6783.75
`the erosion factor the examples apply` MEANS 1.034
`the teacher's stated X after erosion` MEANS 7014.39
`the teacher's coefficient in the example` MEANS 34
`the teacher's stated A`              MEANS 9399.29

-- The example's own steps hold to the agora (its A is 9,399.28 by
-- 1.34 × 7,014.39: the printed 9,399.29 is an agora above).
#ASSERT (sum `the teacher's components`) `is within an agora of` `the teacher's stated total`
#ASSERT (`the teacher's stated total` DIVIDED BY `the teacher's position factor`) `is within an agora of` `the teacher's stated full-position X`
#ASSERT (`the teacher's stated full-position X` TIMES `the erosion factor the examples apply`) `is within an agora of` `the teacher's stated X after erosion`
#ASSERT (`the converted salary` `the teacher's stated X after erosion` `the teacher's coefficient in the example`) `is within an agora of` `the teacher's stated A`

-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-g: the formula as stated, on the example's own X,
-- does not give the example's A: the example multiplies X by 1.034
-- ("תוספת שחיקה"), which neither the formula nor the definition of X has.
-- The reading adopted, as in every conversion circular: the formula as
-- stated, `the converted salary`; the examples' factor stays beside it.
`the formula as stated does not give the examples' A` MEANS
    NOT ((`the converted salary` `the teacher's stated full-position X` 34) `is within an agora of` `the teacher's stated A`)
#ASSERT `the formula as stated does not give the examples' A`

-- 1(ד): placement in the table at the grade whose salary is the nearest
-- at or above A. The example's grade-6 salary ₪9,670.70 is that row.
-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-j: the rule does not say where no grade reaches A.
-- The reading adopted, as in every circular that prints the deputy example
-- below: where none reaches A, the table's highest grade.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p4
GIVEN `table salaries` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc the salaries of the grades at the employee's seniority, in the table
      `converted` IS A NUMBER @desc the salary after conversion (A)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the placement salary` `table salaries` `converted` IS
    IF null (filter (GIVEN s YIELD s AT LEAST `converted`) `table salaries`)
    THEN maximum `table salaries`
    ELSE minimum (filter (GIVEN s YIELD s AT LEAST `converted`) `table salaries`)

#ASSERT 9670.70 AT LEAST `the teacher's stated A`

-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p5 The heading "דגשים".

-- 1(ד) note 2, 2(ג) ¶3, 3(ג) ¶3: on unpaid leave, sabbatical or another
-- unpaid absence in the year before joining, the conversion salary is
-- September's of the year of joining.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p3
GIVEN `absent without pay before joining` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the conversion month` `absent without pay before joining` IS
    IF `absent without pay before joining` THEN "September of the year of joining" ELSE "March of the year before joining"

-- 2: a first deputy. 2(א): the formula; 2(ב): Y = 20%.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b/p2
`a first deputy's coefficient` MEANS 20

-- 2(ג): X is the salary, except the education allowance, refunds, other
