-- 3(ה) ¶4-¶15: for the position beyond 100% (to 150%) a personal
-- supplement: B = T × (100 + Y)/100, T the full salary at the whole
-- position (March of the year before; for an absent principal, March of the
-- year before the absence); C = B − the new tabular salary, turned into a
-- percentage of the combined salary.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p5 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p6 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p7 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p8 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p9 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p10 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p11 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p12 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p13 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p14 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p15
GIVEN T IS A NUMBER, Y IS A NUMBER, `new tabular salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the principal's personal supplement rate` T Y `new tabular salary` IS
    (T TIMES (100 PLUS Y) DIVIDED BY 100 MINUS `new tabular salary`) DIVIDED BY `new tabular salary`

-- ¶16 and steps 1-4: the example's T = 16,314.81 + 6,230.46 = 22,545.27;
-- B − 20,359.87 = 5,567.19. The example stops at step 4 without the
-- percentage (the page ends there); by the rule it is 5,567.19 /
-- 20,359.87, about 27.34%.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p16 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e__cls_1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e__cls_2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e__cls_3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e__cls_4
`the principal example's T` MEANS 16314.81 PLUS 6230.46

#ASSERT `the principal example's T` `is within an agora of` 22545.27
#ASSERT (`the converted salary` 22545.27 `a principal's coefficient` MINUS 20359.87) `is within an agora of` 5567.19
#EVAL `the principal's personal supplement rate` 22545.27 `a principal's coefficient` 20359.87

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Section 9's tables, each inside the range its clause states.
GIVEN rows IS A LIST OF `level row`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the hours in` rows IS map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `level hours`) rows

-- Each table stays inside the range its clause states.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN h YIELD h AT LEAST 6 AND h AT MOST 9) (`the hours in` `the principal's frontal hours by level`)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN h YIELD h AT LEAST 18 AND h AT MOST 21) (`the hours in` `the primary first deputy's frontal hours by level`)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN h YIELD h AT LEAST 9 AND h AT MOST 11) (`the hours in` `the post-primary first deputy's frontal hours by level`)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN h YIELD h AT LEAST 13 AND h AT MOST 15) (`the hours in` `the multi-stage first deputy's frontal hours by level`)

-- Examples of the main rules. The employees are made up.
`an existing academic at 40%` MEANS
    `school employee` WITH
        `recognized teaching seniority`       IS 12
        `academic`                            IS TRUE
        `teaching certificate`                IS TRUE
        `employee's position fraction`        IS 0.4
        `signed the academic-completion undertaking` IS FALSE
        `approved by the exceptions committee` IS FALSE
        `in regular education`                IS FALSE
        `health professions or arts therapist` IS FALSE

`an existing non-academic of 20 years, unsigned` MEANS
    `school employee` WITH
        `recognized teaching seniority`       IS 20
        `academic`                            IS FALSE
        `teaching certificate`                IS TRUE
        `employee's position fraction`        IS 1
        `signed the academic-completion undertaking` IS FALSE
        `approved by the exceptions committee` IS FALSE
        `in regular education`                IS FALSE
        `health professions or arts therapist` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `joins Ofek Hadash` `an existing academic at 40%`
#ASSERT NOT `joins Ofek Hadash` `an existing non-academic of 20 years, unsigned`
#ASSERT `the position base for age` 56 TRUE EQUALS 32
#ASSERT `the position base for age` 56 FALSE EQUALS 34
#ASSERT `the weekly reduction` TRUE 0.85 FALSE EQUALS `hours reduction` 1 1
#ASSERT `the weekly reduction` TRUE 0.95 TRUE EQUALS `hours reduction` 0 5
#ASSERT `the counseling allowance rate` 8 TRUE EQUALS 0.12
#ASSERT `a counselor teaches enough` 6 36 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a counselor teaches enough` 5 36 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a counselor teaches enough` 3 18 TRUE
#ASSERT `a counselor teaches enough` 4 36 FALSE

-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-i: read with the place governing both limbs, a
-- counselor outside primary and junior-high schools has no stated minimum.
GIVEN `teaching hours` IS A NUMBER, `position hours` IS A NUMBER, `in a primary school or junior high` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a counselor teaches enough with both limbs confined to primary and junior high` `teaching hours` `position hours` `in a primary school or junior high` IF
    IF `in a primary school or junior high`
    THEN `teaching hours` AT LEAST `position hours` DIVIDED BY 6 AND `teaching hours` AT LEAST 4
    ELSE TRUE

`the two readings of 13.1 differ for a post-primary counselor` MEANS
        (NOT `a counselor teaches enough` 0 36 FALSE)
    AND `a counselor teaches enough with both limbs confined to primary and junior high` 0 36 FALSE
#ASSERT `the two readings of 13.1 differ for a post-primary counselor`
#ASSERT `the advance rate of` `post-primary teacher` EQUALS 0.27
#ASSERT `work counts from` (7 TIMES 60 PLUS 30) EQUALS 465
#ASSERT `the position may be approved` 1.2 FALSE TRUE TRUE 8 42 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the position may be approved` 1.1 TRUE TRUE TRUE 8 40 FALSE

-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-h: §14.7 prints the grade coordinator's reward as "6% / 7%" under
-- an asterisk, and the circular carries no note for it.
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the rates §14.7 prints for the grade coordinator` IS LIST 0.06, 0.07

GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `the notes the circular gives for the grade coordinator's asterisk` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grade coordinator is given two rates and no rule to choose` IF
        count `the rates §14.7 prints for the grade coordinator` EQUALS 2
    AND `the notes the circular gives for the grade coordinator's asterisk` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the grade coordinator is given two rates and no rule to choose`

-- The undertaking submitted on 25 August 2022: in time under the reading
-- adopted (30.8.2022). Not submitted: breached.
#TRACE `the owner's undertaking` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `submit the owner's undertaking through the portal` AT 8
#TRACE `the owner's undertaking` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `submit the owner's undertaking through the portal` AT 20

-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-l: "בביה"ס יותקן שעון נוכחות" names no one to install it and no
-- date. The reading adopted, as F-2021-22_tashpab_02-n's: no duty to install
-- is encoded; whether the clock is installed decides only how the teachers
-- report.
GIVETH A LIST OF Party
DECIDE `the parties §16.1 names to install the clock` IS EMPTY
`§16.1 names no one to install the clock` MEANS
    `the parties §16.1 names to install the clock` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `§16.1 names no one to install the clock`

-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-m: the advance rows as printed. An intern is a teaching employee
-- who is not a principal or a first deputy, so in each stage two rows price
-- the intern (27% and 22% post-primary, 17% and 14% primary). The reading
-- adopted, as F-2021-22_tashpab_02-m's: the row that names interns governs
-- them, as the advance rate above is encoded.
DECLARE `printed post-primary advance row` IS ONE OF
    `teachers who are not principals or first deputies`, `interns`, `first deputies`, `principals`
DECLARE `role for the printed rows` IS ONE OF `a teacher`, `an intern`, `a first deputy`, `a principal`
GIVEN row IS A `printed post-primary advance row`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the rate the printed row gives` row IS
    CONSIDER row
    WHEN `teachers who are not principals or first deputies` THEN 0.27
    WHEN `interns` THEN 0.22
    WHEN `first deputies` THEN 0.20
    WHEN `principals` THEN 0.15
GIVEN row IS A `printed post-primary advance row`, r IS A `role for the printed rows`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the printed row covers` row r IF
    CONSIDER row
    WHEN `teachers who are not principals or first deputies` THEN NOT (r EQUALS `a first deputy` OR r EQUALS `a principal`)
    WHEN `interns` THEN r EQUALS `an intern`
    WHEN `first deputies` THEN r EQUALS `a first deputy`
    WHEN `principals` THEN r EQUALS `a principal`
`a post-primary intern has two advance rates` MEANS
    map (GIVEN row YIELD `the rate the printed row gives` row)
        (filter (GIVEN row YIELD `the printed row covers` row `an intern`)
                (LIST `teachers who are not principals or first deputies`, `interns`, `first deputies`, `principals`))
    EQUALS LIST 0.27, 0.22
#ASSERT `a post-primary intern has two advance rates`

-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-n: §6.2's first three criteria are needs (a required subject, a
-- shortage in the area, a remote locality) and the list does not say
-- whether they are cumulative. The reading adopted, as
-- F-2021-22_tashpab_02-b's: alternatives, any one of them grounding the
-- request (the input `a criterion of 6.2 is met`).
GIVEN `required subject` IS A BOOLEAN, `shortage in the area` IS A BOOLEAN, `remote locality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `6.2's needs, read as alternatives` `required subject` `shortage in the area` `remote locality` IF
    `required subject` OR `shortage in the area` OR `remote locality`
GIVEN `required subject` IS A BOOLEAN, `shortage in the area` IS A BOOLEAN, `remote locality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `6.2's needs, read together` `required subject` `shortage in the area` `remote locality` IF
    `required subject` AND `shortage in the area` AND `remote locality`
`the two readings of the criteria decide one request differently` MEANS
        `6.2's needs, read as alternatives` TRUE FALSE FALSE
    AND (NOT `6.2's needs, read together` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the two readings of the criteria decide one request differently`

-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-o: 3.3.1 binds "up to 27 years (inclusive)" and 3.3.2 frees "28
-- years and above"; seniority of 27 and a half years is in neither as
-- printed. The reading adopted, as F-2021-22_tashpab_02-l's: whole years —
-- one who has not completed 28 is "up to 27" and must sign, as the joining
-- rule above is encoded.
GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in 3.3.1's printed band` s IF s AT MOST 27
GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in 3.3.2's printed band` s IF s AT LEAST 28
`a non-academic teacher of 27 and a half years is in neither rule` MEANS
    (NOT `in 3.3.1's printed band` 27.5) AND NOT `in 3.3.2's printed band` 27.5
#ASSERT `a non-academic teacher of 27 and a half years is in neither rule`

-- F-2022-23_tashpag_02-p: 2.1(2)(ב) has unreported employees open a file "urgently" and
-- names no day. The reading adopted, as F-2024-25_tashpah_01-n's: the duty
-- is encoded without a deadline.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the days 2.1(2)(ב) gives for "urgently"` IS NOTHING

`"urgently" names no deadline` MEANS
    `the days 2.1(2)(ב) gives for "urgently"` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `"urgently" names no deadline`

§§ `Property checks`

-- The circular over finite spaces, section by section.

`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE
`hundredths to 1` MEANS map (GIVEN k YIELD k DIVIDED BY 100) (range 0 100)
`positions checked` MEANS LIST 0.25, 1 DIVIDED BY 3, 0.4, 0.5, 0.75, 1
`every week kind` MEANS LIST `special-education primary teacher`, `special-education primary health professional`, `special-education post-primary teacher`, `special-education post-primary health professional`
`every level table` MEANS LIST `the principal's frontal hours by level`, `the primary first deputy's frontal hours by level`, `the post-primary first deputy's frontal hours by level`, `the multi-stage first deputy's frontal hours by level`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, a IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, p IS A NUMBER, d IS A BOOLEAN, x IS A BOOLEAN, r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `school employee`
DECIDE `a checked employee` y a c p d x r IS
    `school employee` WITH
        `recognized teaching seniority`              IS y
        `academic`                                   IS a
        `teaching certificate`                       IS c
        `employee's position fraction`               IS p
        `signed the academic-completion undertaking` IS d
        `approved by the exceptions committee`       IS x
        `in regular education`                       IS r
        `health professions or arts therapist`       IS FALSE

-- §3.2.1 and §3.4 over every flag and position: an existing academic joins
-- exactly from a third, certified or by exception; a new one exactly from a
-- third (half in regular education) and certified.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD
                all (GIVEN x YIELD
                        all (GIVEN r YIELD
                                all (GIVEN p YIELD
                                            `joins Ofek Hadash` (`a checked employee` 5 TRUE c p FALSE x r)
                                            EQUALS (p AT LEAST 1 DIVIDED BY 3 AND (c OR x))
                                        AND `joins Ofek Hadash` (`a checked employee` 0 TRUE c p FALSE x r)
                                            EQUALS (p AT LEAST (IF r THEN 0.5 ELSE 1 DIVIDED BY 3) AND c))
                                    `positions checked`)
                            `both booleans`)
                    `both booleans`)
            `both booleans`

-- §3.3 and §12.2.3 over seniority 20 to 35: an existing non-academic joins,
-- and is promoted, exactly from 28 years or on signing (or the degree).
#ASSERT all (GIVEN s YIELD
                all (GIVEN d YIELD
                            `joins Ofek Hadash` (`a checked employee` s FALSE TRUE 1 d FALSE FALSE) EQUALS (s AT LEAST 28 OR d)
                        AND `a non-academic may be promoted` (`a checked employee` s FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE) d EQUALS (s AT LEAST 28 OR d))
                    `both booleans`)
            (range 20 35)

-- §4 over every week kind and position: the week is 36 hours and adds up;
-- a part position is the full week's share; the primary week is the one of
-- a primary school and of grades 1-6.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN k YIELD
                all (GIVEN p YIELD
                        LET w MEANS `the part-time work week of` k p
                        IN      (`the work week of` k)'s `week hours` EQUALS 36
                            AND (`the work week of` k)'s `frontal hours` PLUS (`the work week of` k)'s `individual hours` PLUS (`the work week of` k)'s `stay hours` EQUALS 36
                            AND w's `frontal hours` PLUS w's `individual hours` PLUS w's `stay hours` EQUALS 36 TIMES p)
                    `positions checked`)
            `every week kind`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD
                    `on the primary work week` TRUE g
                AND `on the primary work week` FALSE g EQUALS (g AT MOST 6))
            (range 1 12)

-- §5.4-§6 over positions in hundredths: a period counts exactly from a
-- third; 5.4 permits at most two schools and 100%; section 6 approves above
-- 100% only on a criterion, frontal, within 8.5 a day and 42 a week, and
-- above 117% only with headquarters.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD
                    `the period counts for promotion` f EQUALS (f AT LEAST 1 DIVIDED BY 3)
                AND all (GIVEN n YIELD
                            `within 5.4` n (f PLUS 0.5) FALSE EQUALS (n AT MOST 2 AND f PLUS 0.5 AT MOST 1))
                        (range 1 4))
            `hundredths to 1`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD
                all (GIVEN cr YIELD
                        all (GIVEN hq YIELD
                                `the position may be approved` (t DIVIDED BY 100) FALSE cr TRUE 8 40 hq
                                EQUALS (t AT MOST 100 OR (cr AND (t AT MOST 117 OR hq))))
                            `both booleans`)
                    `both booleans`)
            (range 90 140)

-- §7 over positions in hundredths: the nursing hours exactly from 90%
-- within four months, the mother's reduction from 79% otherwise, both
-- clauses only at exactly 90% (finding e).
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD
                all (GIVEN m YIELD
                        all (GIVEN w YIELD
                                LET r MEANS `the weekly reduction` m f w
                                IN      (r's `stay reduced` EQUALS 5) EQUALS (w AND f AT LEAST 0.9)
                                    AND (r's `frontal reduced` EQUALS 1) EQUALS ((NOT (w AND f AT LEAST 0.9)) AND m AND f AT LEAST 0.79))
                            `both booleans`)
                    `both booleans`)
            `hundredths to 1`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD (`in 7.3's range` f AND `in 7.4's range` f) EQUALS (f EQUALS 0.9)) `hundredths to 1`

-- §8 over ages 45 to 65: the base is 32, 34 or 36, never rising with age,
-- never higher for an existing teacher; two bases only at 55 for an
-- existing teacher (finding f).
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD
                all (GIVEN ex YIELD
                            elem (`the position base for age` n ex) (LIST 32, 34, 36)
                        AND `the position base for age` (n PLUS 1) ex AT MOST `the position base for age` n ex
                        AND `the position base for age` n TRUE AT MOST `the position base for age` n FALSE
                        AND (count (nub (`the bases the clauses give` n ex)) EQUALS 2) EQUALS (ex AND n EQUALS 55))
                    `both booleans`)
            (range 45 65)

-- §9 over computed levels 0 to 10: the level is 3 to 8; every table names
-- each level 3 to 8 once and never gives more frontal hours at a higher
-- level; the reductions for a mother and age are 0, 2 or 4.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN l YIELD
                LET v MEANS `the complexity level of a special-education school` l
                IN v AT LEAST 3 AND v AT MOST 8)
            (range 0 10)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD
                all (GIVEN l YIELD
                            count (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `level` EQUALS l) t) EQUALS 1
                        AND all (GIVEN r YIELD
                                    all (GIVEN q YIELD
                                            (NOT (r's `level` LESS THAN q's `level`)) OR q's `level hours` AT MOST r's `level hours`)
                                        t)
                                t)
                    (range 3 8))
            `every level table`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN mo YIELD
                all (GIVEN n YIELD elem (`a principal's non-frontal hours reduced` mo n) (LIST 0, 2, 4)) (range 40 65))
            `both booleans`

-- §10 over hours per purpose: within the caps exactly when each purpose is
-- within its own (4, 8, 6), and those add up to the half-year's 18.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN a YIELD
                all (GIVEN b YIELD
                        all (GIVEN c YIELD
                                `a half-year's activity hours are within the caps` a b c EQUALS (a AT MOST 4 AND b AT MOST 8 AND c AT MOST 6))
                            (range 0 7))
                    (range 0 9))
            (range 0 5)

-- §12.2.2 over seniority 20 to 30: two answers exactly at 25 (finding b);
-- an uncertified existing academic may be promoted exactly from 25, and is
-- barred by §3.2.1 exactly below it.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN s YIELD
                    (count (`what 12.2.2's two groups say of seniority` s) EQUALS 2) EQUALS (s EQUALS 25)
                AND `an uncertified academic may be promoted` (`a checked employee` s TRUE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS (s AT LEAST 25)
                AND `cannot be promoted until certified under 3.2.1` (`a checked employee` s TRUE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS (s LESS THAN 25))
            (range 20 30)

-- §13: a counselor of a full position always needs 4 teaching hours; the
-- allowance needs 7 counselling hours.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN h YIELD
                all (GIVEN pj YIELD
                        (NOT `a counselor teaches enough` h 36 pj) OR h AT LEAST 4)
                    `both booleans`)
            (range 0 10)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN h YIELD
                all (GIVEN l YIELD (`the counseling allowance rate` h l GREATER THAN 0) EQUALS (h AT LEAST 7)) `both booleans`)
            (range 0 12)

-- §14.5 over quarter grades; §15.2: every advance rate between 14% and
-- 27%, interns below teachers in both stages.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN k YIELD
                `a grade the conversion may give` (k DIVIDED BY 4) EQUALS (FLOOR (k DIVIDED BY 2) TIMES 2 EQUALS k))
            (range 0 40)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD `the advance rate of` g AT LEAST 0.14 AND `the advance rate of` g AT MOST 0.27)
            (LIST `primary teacher`, `primary intern`, `post-primary teacher`, `post-primary intern`, `first deputy`, `principal`)
`interns are advanced less than teachers` MEANS
        `the advance rate of` `primary intern` LESS THAN `the advance rate of` `primary teacher`
    AND `the advance rate of` `post-primary intern` LESS THAN `the advance rate of` `post-primary teacher`
#ASSERT `interns are advanced less than teachers`

-- §16.2 over clock-ins from 6:00 to 9:00: work never counts before 7:45.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD
                    `work counts from` t AT LEAST 465
                AND (`work counts from` t EQUALS t) EQUALS (t AT LEAST 465))
            (range 360 540)
